{"id":"hivites","name":"Hivites","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","torrey","easton"],"topics":["nave:hivites","torrey:hivites"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Hivites","text":"One of the original tribes scattered over Palestine, from Hermon to Gibeon in the south. The name is interpreted as “midlanders” or “villagers” (Gen. 10:17; 1 Chr. 1:15). They were probably a branch of the Hittites. At the time of Jacob’s return to Canaan, Hamor the Hivite was the “prince of the land” (Gen. 24:2-28). They are next mentioned during the Conquest (Josh. 9:7; 11:19). They principally inhabited the northern confines of Western Palestine (Josh. 11:3; Judg. 3:3). A remnant of them still existed in the time of Solomon (1 Kings 9:20)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H2340","lemma":"חִוִּי","xlit":"Chivvîy","gloss":"a Chivvite, one of the aboriginal tribes of Palestine","kjv":"Hivite","count":19,"share":0.68},{"strong":"H2850","lemma":"חִתִּי","xlit":"Chittîy","gloss":"a Chittite, or descendant of Cheth","kjv":"Hittite, Hittities","count":13,"share":0.46},{"strong":"H3669","lemma":"כְּנַעַנִי","xlit":"Kᵉnaʻanîy","gloss":"a Kenaanite or inhabitant of Kenaan","kjv":"Canaanite, merchant, trafficker","count":13,"share":0.46},{"strong":"H6522","lemma":"פְּרִזִּי","xlit":"Pᵉrizzîy","gloss":"a Perizzite, one of the Canaanitish tribes","kjv":"Perizzite","count":10,"share":0.36},{"strong":"H2983","lemma":"יְבוּסִי","xlit":"Yᵉbûwçîy","gloss":"a Jebusite or inhabitant of Jebus","kjv":"Jebusite","count":10,"share":0.36},{"strong":"H567","lemma":"אֱמֹרִי","xlit":"ʼĔmôrîy","gloss":"an Emorite, one of the Canaanitish tribes","kjv":"Amorite","count":10,"share":0.36}],"verses":["Gen.10.17","Gen.34.2","Gen.36.2","Exod.3.8","Exod.23.23","Exod.23.28","Deut.7.1","Deut.20.17","Josh.9.1","Josh.9.7","Josh.11.3","Josh.11.19","Josh.12.8","Josh.24.11","Judg.3.3","Judg.3.5","2Sam.24.7","1Kgs.9.20","1Chr.1.15","Gen.10.15","Gen.26.34","Deut.2.33","Deut.7.2","Deut.7.24","Josh.9.3","Josh.13.3","1Kgs.9.21","2